Protodoc Specification Licence (Draft v0.1)
Status: DRAFT -- pending Eyvar Garcia's review and approval (see GOVERNANCE.md
and specs/CHANGES.md for the approval record once it exists; this document
records no approval of its own).

This licence covers the Protodoc specification text and reference materials
in this repository under specs/001-protodoc-format-core/ and
.specify/memory/constitution.md (the "Specification"), and, separately, the
patent claims described in Section 2 below. It does not cover this
repository's reference-implementation source code (pkg/, cmd/), which is
licensed separately under LICENSE-CODE (Apache License 2.0), decided
2026-09-19.

1. Copyright licence (Specification text)

   Subject to the terms of this licence, the copyright holder grants to
   every person obtaining a copy of the Specification a worldwide,
   royalty-free, non-exclusive, irrevocable licence to reproduce, prepare
   derivative works of, publicly display, publicly perform, sublicense and
   distribute the Specification, provided that:

   a. this licence notice and the copyright notice are retained in all
      copies or substantial portions of the Specification; and
   b. a derivative work that modifies the normative requirements of the
      Specification is clearly marked as a derivative and not represented
      as the Specification itself.

2. Patent licence (irrevocable, royalty-free)

   Subject to the terms of this licence, each contributor to the
   Specification grants to every person who implements, in whole or in
   part, any version of the Specification a worldwide, royalty-free,
   non-exclusive, irrevocable (except as stated in Section 2(a)) licence
   under that contributor's necessary patent claims -- those patent claims
   a contributor owns or controls that are necessarily infringed by
   implementing the normative portions of the Specification, with no
   reasonable non-infringing alternative -- to make, use, sell, offer for
   sale, import and otherwise dispose of a conforming implementation of the
   Specification.

   a. This patent licence extends to a given implementer only for so long
      as that implementer does not assert, in litigation or a formal
      demand, that a conforming implementation of the Specification (by
      any party) infringes a patent claim owned or controlled by that
      implementer. Asserting such a claim terminates the patent licence
      granted to that implementer under this Section 2, but has no effect
      on any other implementer's licence.
   b. This patent licence survives a contributor ceasing to participate in
      the Specification's governance; it cannot be revoked by a change of
      steward, a change of governance process, or the Specification
      reaching or leaving any particular status (draft, stable,
      deprecated).

3. No trademark licence

   This licence does not grant rights to use the "Protodoc" name, or any
   associated logo, to endorse or promote an implementation, except to
   truthfully describe the origin of the Specification an implementation
   conforms to.

4. Disclaimer of warranty

   THE SPECIFICATION IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,
   EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF
   MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.
   IN NO EVENT SHALL A CONTRIBUTOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR
   OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE
   SPECIFICATION OR ANY IMPLEMENTATION OF IT.

5. Governance cross-reference

   The named steward, succession arrangement and deprecation-window policy
   required alongside this licence by CON-026 are recorded in GOVERNANCE.md
   in this repository, not in this file, so that a governance-process change
   never requires re-issuing the licence text itself.

